# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AgenticCore .gitignore
#
# These rules ship with the framework and are inherited by adopters
# (export-framework.sh copies the framework tree into the adopter repo).
# They fall into two classes:
#
#   UNIVERSAL — machine-local config / secrets / build output. Never commit in
#   ANY repo (framework or adopter). An adopter must NOT un-ignore these.
#
#   FRAMEWORK-BENCH — bench/worktree mechanics that the framework and adopters
#   both use (benches are git worktrees, relay notes, session logs). Regenerable.
#
# Adopters manage their OWN project-specific ignores on top of this file;
# export-framework.sh never writes an adopter's .gitignore for customer paths.
# See mddocs/reference.architecture/bootstrap-new-project.md for the adoption
# inheritance note.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- UNIVERSAL -----------------------------------------------------------

# Ephemeral / scratch working directory (project-local). Durable rule: do
# throwaway work in ./.tmp at the project root, not /tmp. Never committed.
# (The workspace-root AgenticCore.v0.5/.tmp lives outside this repo; this rule
# also guards any .tmp created inside the repo.)
.tmp/

# Nested git repositories (sub-projects / worktrees that contain their own .git)
**/.git/

# Machine-local agentic tool settings — never commit
.mcp.json
opencode.json.local
.agentic/

# mdBook build output
mddocs/book/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Environment / credential injection — see .envrc.template
# .envrc is never committed (ADR-0001 D-2, ADR-0021 D-4) — .envrc.template is the reference
.envrc
.envrc.local

# Machine-local env var overrides (never commit)
# .env-required itself is committed — only var names, no values
.env-required.local

# Archive and packaging artifacts
*.tgz
*.tgz.sha256
*.tgz.toc

# macOS filesystem metadata
.DS_Store

# Review-ledger runtime data (findings) — machine-local audit entries.
# The framework's own authoring does NOT utilize the review-ledger; adopters get
# both ledgers (security + reviews) wired and ready. The .gitkeep files that
# create the directories remain tracked.
.core/review-ledger/**/findings.yaml

# --- FRAMEWORK-BENCH -------------------------------------------------------

# Git worktree directories (ephemeral benches)
.worktrees/
worktrees/

# Bench artifacts — relay-pending.md and .bench/ are worktree-local (written by provision-bench.sh), regenerable, never committed; canonical bench provenance lives in bench-registry.yaml (AP-056, ADR-0015 amendment)
relay-pending.md
.bench/

# Out-of-band scratch logs (tracked for audit recovery only)
_oob/*.log

# Session reasoning logs (append-only, machine-local, never committed)
_scratch/sessions/
